# RepoLens

Build a shared knowledge platform for GitHub repositories covering source code, docs, issues, PRs, comments, releases, and development history.

Source-code indexing is in scope. The previous history-only restriction is superseded.

The previous local setup has been cleared. Treat all product capabilities as planned until implemented and verified in the current checkout.

Preserve evidence provenance and repository/version boundaries. Answers should cite supporting evidence and acknowledge missing evidence. Keep private data permission-scoped if private repositories are introduced.

Choose architecture and integrations based on the rebuild requirements. Do not treat previous resume bullets as proof of implementation. Demonstrate improvements over an LLM connected to GitHub through comparable evaluations.
